mn26:25.18 starts: To set rolling the wheel of Dhamma
mn26:25.19 starts: I go to the city of Kāsi.
mn26:25.20 starts: In a world become blind,
mn26:25.21 starts: I beat the drum of the deathless.’
mn49:9.1 starts: “‘As far as suns & moons revolve,
mn49:9.2 starts: shining, illuminating the directions,
mn49:9.3 starts: over a thousand-fold world
mn49:9.4 starts: your control holds sway.
mn85:49.19 starts: To set rolling the wheel of Dhamma
mn85:49.20 starts: I go to the city of Kāsi.
mn85:49.21 starts: In a world become blind,
mn85:49.22 starts: I beat the drum of the deathless.’
mn82:25.17 starts: Like a newly painted unguent pot—
mn82:25.18 starts: a putrid body adorned:
mn82:25.19 starts: enough to deceive a fool,
mn82:25.20 starts: but not a seeker for the further shore.
mn82:42.19 starts: So he burns, poked with sticks,
mn82:42.20 starts: in just one piece of cloth,
mn82:42.21 starts: They are not shelters for one who
mn82:42.22 starts: not relatives,
mn82:42.35 starts: Thus the discernment by which
mn82:42.36 starts: one attains to mastery,
mn82:42.37 starts: for those who haven’t reached mastery
mn82:42.38 starts: out of delusion,
mn85:43.8 starts: ‘Enough now with teaching
mn85:43.9 starts: what
mn85:43.10 starts: This Dhamma is not easily realized
mn85:43.11 starts: by those overcome
